{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:2","rows":[{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hamd is praise of the praised one’s beautiful attributes and actions, while shukr is praise for a favor; every shukr is hamd but not every hamd is shukr, so God may praise Himself but not thank Himself.","anchor":"فهو الثناء على المحمود بجميل صفاته وأفعاله والشكر الثناء عليه بإنعامه فكل شكر حمد وليس كل حمد شكرا"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hamd differs from madh: hamd is deserved only for a good act, while madh may praise an act or a non-action; all hamd is madh, but not vice versa.","anchor":"أن الحمد لا يستحق إلا على فعل حسن والمدح قد يكون على فعل وغير فعل فكل حمد مدح وليس كل مدح حمدا"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God may be praised for knowledge and power but not hamd for them, since they are attributes of essence; He may be praised and hamd for creating and providing, attributes of action.","anchor":"جاز أن يمدح الله تعالى على صفته بأنه عالم قادر ولم يجز أن يحمد به لأن العلم والقدرة من صفات ذاته"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One derivation of rabb is owner, as in the owner of a house.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من المالك كما يقال رب الدار أي مالكها"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another derivation is master; 12:41 calls a human master rabb.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من السيد لأن السيد يسمى ربا قال تعالى أما أحدكما فيسقي ربه خمرا","mentions":["12:41"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third meaning is manager; rabbani scholars are so called for managing people through knowledge, and a housewife is called rabbat al-bayt for managing the home.","anchor":"أن الرب المدبر ومنه قول الله عز وجل والربانيون والأحبار وهم العلماء سموا ربانيين لقيامهم بتدبير الناس بعلمهم","mentions":["5:44"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth derivation connects rabb to nurturing; stepchildren are named rabائب because the husband raises them, as in 4:23.","anchor":"الرب مشتق من التربية ومنه قوله تعالى وربائبكم اللاتي في حجوركم فسمي ولد الزوجة ربيبة لتربية الزوج لها","mentions":["4:23"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"If rabb means owner or master, it describes God’s essence; if it means manager or nurturer, it describes His action.","anchor":"فعلى هذا أن صفة الله تعالى بأنه رب لأنه مالك أو سيد فذلك صفة من صفات ذاته وإن قيل لأنه مدبر لخلقه أو مربيهم"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"With the definite article, rabb is exclusive to God; without it, the word is shared by God and His servants.","anchor":"ومتى أدخلت عليه الألف واللام اختص الله تعالى به دون عباده وإن حذفتا منه صار مشتركا بين الله وبين عباده"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-alamin is the plural of alam, with no singular of the same form, like raht and qawm; each age or community is an alam, as the cited al-A‘raj verse illustrates.","anchor":"فهو جمع عالم لا واحد له من لفظه مثل رهط وقوم وأهل كل زمان عالم قال العجاج"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas takes the worlds to mean rational beings: angels, humans, and jinn.","anchor":"أنه ما يعقل من الملائكة والإنس والجن وهذا قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view takes the worlds to mean the present world and all it contains.","anchor":"أن العالم الدنيا وما فيها"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"أبو إسحاق الزجاج","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Zajjaj takes the worlds to include everything God created in this world and the afterlife.","anchor":"أن العالم كل ما خلقه الله تعالى في الدنيا والآخرة وهذا قول أبي إسحاق الزجاج"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The derivation from knowledge fits the interpretation that alam means rational beings.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من العلم وهذا تأويل من جعل العالم اسما لما يعقل"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The alternative derivation is from sign, since the worlds are signs pointing to their creator; this fits the interpretation that alam means all created things.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من العلامة لأنه دلالة على خالقه وهذا تأويل من جعل العالم اسما لكل مخلوق"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:3","rows":[],"none":"verse text only"}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:5","rows":[{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["إِيَّاكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الخليل","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Khalil says the divine name is annexed to the pronoun kaf in iyyaka.","anchor":"أن اسم الله تعالى مضاف إلى الكاف وهذا قول الخليل"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["إِيَّاكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الأخفش","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Akhfash takes iyyaka as a single pronoun for God, not an annexation, because a pronoun is not annexed.","anchor":"أنها كلمة واحدة كني بها عن اسم الله تعالى وليس فيها إضافة لأن المضمر لا يضاف وهذا قول الأخفش"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"prefers","claim":"The clearest sense of worship is humility, the highest form of submission, owed only to God as giver of the greatest gifts such as life, reason, hearing, and sight.","anchor":"أن العبادة الخضوع ولا يستحقها إلا الله تعالى لأنها أعلى مراتب الخضوع فلا يستحقها إلا المنعم بأعظم النعم"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A second interpretation takes worship to mean obedience.","anchor":"أن العبادة الطاعة"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third interpretation takes worship to mean drawing near through obedience.","anchor":"أنها التقرب بالطاعة"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Humility is clearest because Christians worshipped Jesus without obeying him through worship, while the Prophet is obeyed but is not thereby worshipped.","anchor":"لأن النصارى عبدت عيسى عليه السلام ولم تطعه بالعبادة والنبي صلى الله عليه وسلم مطاع وليس بمعبود بالطاعة"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:6","rows":[{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation of ihdina is guide us and show us the way.","anchor":"معناه أرشدنا ودلنا"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas interprets ihdina as grant us success.","anchor":"معناه وفقنا وهذا قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Sirat can mean the straight path, illustrated by Jarir’s verse about the commander being on a straight course when routes bend.","anchor":"أنه السبيل المستقيم ومنه قول جرير أمير المؤمنين على صراط إذا اعوج الموارد مستقيم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Sirat can also mean a clear road, as in 7:86 and the cited verse about turning from the clear path.","anchor":"أنه الطريق الواضح ومنه قوله تعالى ولا تقعدوا بكل صراط توعدون وقال الشاعر","mentions":["7:86"]},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Sirat derives from the passage of food as it moves through the throat.","anchor":"وهو مشتق من مسترط الطعام وهو ممره في الحلق"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The already guided ask for guidance to continue and remain constant.","anchor":"أنهم دعوا باستدامة الهداية وإن كانوا قد هدوا"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Alternatively, the prayer asks God to increase their guidance.","anchor":"معناه زدنا هداية"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third view sees the request as sincere desire for guidance and hope for the reward of prayer.","anchor":"دعوا بها إخلاصا للرغبة ورجاء لثواب الدعاء"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"علي وعبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Ali and Abdullah identify the straight path as God’s Book; a similar interpretation is attributed to the Prophet.","anchor":"أنه كتاب الله تعالى وهو قول علي وعبد الله ويروى نحوه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"A report attributed to the Prophet likewise identifies the straight path as God’s Book; no grading is given.","anchor":"ويروى نحوه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"جابر بن عبد الله ومحمد بن الحنفية","stance":"reports","claim":"Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya identify the straight path as Islam.","anchor":"أنه الإسلام وهو قول جابر بن عبد الله ومحمد بن الحنفية"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas identifies it as the way guiding to God’s religion, without any crookedness.","anchor":"أنه الطريق الهادي إلى دين الله تعالى الذي لا عوج فيه وهو قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"الحسن البصري وأبو العالية الرياحي","stance":"reports","claim":"Hasan al-Basri and Abu al-Aliya al-Riyahi identify the path as the Messenger and the best of his family and Companions.","anchor":"هو رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وأخيار أهل بيته وأصحابه وهو قول الحسن البصري وأبي العالية الرياحي"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:7","rows":[{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One view identifies those favored as the angels.","anchor":"أحدها أنهم الملائكة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view identifies those favored as the prophets.","anchor":"والثاني أنهم الأنبياء"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view identifies them as believers in earlier scriptures.","anchor":"والثالث أنهم المؤمنون بالكتب السالفة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"وكيع","stance":"reports","claim":"Waki‘ identifies them as Muslims.","anchor":"والرابع أنهم المسلمون وهو قول وكيع"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"عبد الرحمن بن زيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd identifies them as the Prophet and his Companions.","anchor":"هم النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ومن معه من أصحابه وهذا قول عبد الرحمن بن زيد"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["صِرَٰطَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"عمر بن الخطاب وعبد الله بن الزبير","stance":"reports","claim":"Umar ibn al-Khattab and Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr read min an‘amta alayhim instead of alladhina an‘amta alayhim.","anchor":"وقرأ عمر بن الخطاب وعبد الله بن الزبير صراط من أنعمت عليهم"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عدي بن حاتم","stance":"reports","claim":"Adi ibn Hatim reports that the Prophet identified those under wrath as Jews and those astray as Christians; al-Mawardi says all exegetes agree.","anchor":"روى عن عدي بن حاتم قال سألت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم عن المغضوب عليهم فقال هم اليهود وعن الضالين فقال هم النصارى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-Mawardi says all exegetes agree that those under wrath are Jews and those astray are Christians.","anchor":"وهو قول جميع المفسرين"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation takes God’s wrath in its familiar sense as anger among people.","anchor":"الغضب المعروف من العباد"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation takes wrath as the will to exact vengeance, since the linguistic root implies harshness, which cannot be ascribed to God.","anchor":"أنه إرادة الانتقام لأن أصل الغضب في اللغة هو الغلظة وهذه الصفة لا تجوز على الله تعالى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third interpretation is that God’s wrath means His condemnation of them.","anchor":"أن غضبه عليهم هو ذمه لهم"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth interprets wrath as a kind of punishment named anger, just as God’s blessings are named mercy.","anchor":"أنه نوع من العقوبة سمي غضبا كما سميت نعمه رحمة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلضَّآلِّينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Misguidance is the opposite of guidance.","anchor":"والضلال ضد الهدى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God singles out Jews as the objects of wrath because they are the most hostile.","anchor":"وخص الله تعالى اليهود بالغضب لأنهم أشد عداوة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"عمر بن الخطاب","stance":"reports","claim":"Umar ibn al-Khattab reads ghayr before al-dallin as well, repeating ghayr in the phrase.","anchor":"وقرأ عمر بن الخطاب غير المغضوب عليهم وغير الضالين"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:1","rows":[{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["*"],"type":"sciences","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-A‘la is Meccan by agreement.","anchor":"سورة الأعلى مكية باتفاق"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس والسدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas and al-Suddi interpret sabbih as glorify your Lord Most High; ism is an added word intended to exalt the named one, as Labid’s verse illustrates.","anchor":"عظم ربك الأعلى قاله ابن عباس والسدي والاسم صلة قصد بها تعظيم المسمى كما قال لبيد"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الطبري","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Tabari interprets the command as declaring the Lord’s name too exalted to be given to anyone else.","anchor":"نزه اسم ربك عن أن يسمى به أحد سواه ذكره الطبري"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation is to raise one’s voice in remembrance of the Lord, supported by Jarir’s verse about pilgrims chanting and magnifying God.","anchor":"معناه ارفع صوتك بذكر ربك قال جرير قبح الإله وجوه تغلب كلما سبح الحجيج وكبروا تكبيرا"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth interpretation is pray to your Lord.","anchor":"الرابع صل لربك"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"On the prayer interpretation, ism rabbika can mean by your Lord’s command.","anchor":"بأمر ربك"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"It can instead mean by mentioning your Lord at the opening of prayer.","anchor":"بذكر ربك أن تفتتح به الصلاة"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"It can also mean keeping the Lord in one’s heart while intending the prayer.","anchor":"أن تكون ذاكرا لربك بقلبك في نيتك للصلاة"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"علي وابن عباس وابن عمر","stance":"reports","claim":"Ali, Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Umar would say Glory be to my Lord Most High when beginning the sura’s recitation, acting on its opening command.","anchor":"وروي أن عليا وابن عباس وابن عمر كانوا إذا افتتحوا قراءة هذه السورة قالوا سبحان ربي الأعلى امتثالا لأمره تعالى في ابتدائها"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبي وابن عمر","stance":"reports","claim":"It is said that Ubay’s reading has Glory be to my Lord Most High in place of the opening words, and Ibn Umar recited it that way.","anchor":"وقيل إنها في قراءة أبي سبحان ربي الأعلى وكان ابن عمر يقرؤها كذلك"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:2","rows":[{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One possibility is that God brought people into being and then perfected them.","anchor":"يعني أنشأ خلقهم ثم سواهم فأكملهم"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another is that He created them fully and made each limb proportionate to its counterpart.","anchor":"خلقهم خلقا كاملا وسوى لكل جارحة مثلا"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third is that He created them through His favor and equalized them in His rulings; al-Dahhak specifies that He created Adam and fashioned his form.","anchor":"خلقهم بإنعامه وسوى بينهم في أحكامه قال الضحاك خلق آدم فسوى خلقه"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth possibility is that He created in men’s loins and fashioned in mothers’ wombs.","anchor":"خلق في أصلاب الرجال وسوى في أرحام الأمهات"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fifth possibility is that He created bodies and fashioned understandings.","anchor":"خلق الأجساد فسوى الأفهام"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:3","rows":[{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujahid says God decreed misery and happiness, and guided toward right conduct and misguidance.","anchor":"قدر الشقاوة والسعادة وهداه للرشد والضلالة قاله مجاهد"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view says God apportioned provisions and food, and guided humans to their livelihood and wild animals to their pastures.","anchor":"قدر أرزاقهم وأقواتهم وهداهم لمعاشهم إن كانوا إنسا ولمراعيهم إن كانوا وحشا"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"السدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Suddi says God made them male and female and guided the male in approaching the female.","anchor":"قدرهم ذكورا وإناثا وهدى الذكر كيف يأتي الأنثى قاله السدي"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth possibility is that God determined their formation in the womb and guided them to emerge fully formed.","anchor":"قدر خلقهم في الأرحام وهداهم الخروج للتمام"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fifth possibility is that God created them for recompense and guided them to action.","anchor":"خلقهم للجزاء وهداهم للعمل"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:6","rows":[{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["فَلَا تَنسَىٰٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation takes do not forget to mean do not abandon the work, except where God grants a concession; on this reading the phrase prohibits associating partners with God.","anchor":"أن معنى قوله فلا تنسى أي فلا تترك العمل إلا ما شاء الله أن يترخص لك فيه فعلى هذا التأويل يكون هذا نهيا عن الشرك"},{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["سَنُقْرِئُكَ فَلَا تَنسَىٰٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The other interpretation is God’s assurance that the Prophet will not forget the Qur’an He recites to him.","anchor":"أنه إخبار من الله تعالى أنه لا ينسى ما يقرئه من القرآن"},{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["سَنُقْرِئُكَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas relates that the Prophet repeated Gabriel’s revelation for fear of forgetting, so God revealed that He would recite the Qur’an to him and he would not forget; no grading is given.","anchor":"حكى ابن عباس أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم كان إذا نزل عليه جبريل بالوحي يقرؤه خيفة أن ينساه فأنزل الله تعالى سنقرئك فلا تنسى"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:12","rows":[{"verses":["87:12"],"words":["ٱلنَّارَ ٱلْكُبْرَىٰ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"يحيى بن سلام","stance":"reports","claim":"Yahya ibn Sallam identifies the greater fire as Hell and the lesser fire as the fire of this world.","anchor":"هي نار جهنم والصغرى نار الدنيا قاله يحيى بن سلام"},{"verses":["87:12"],"words":["ٱلنَّارَ ٱلْكُبْرَىٰ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farra’s interpretation identifies the greater fire as the disbelievers’ fire in Hell’s lowest level and the lesser fire as sinners’ fire in its upper level.","anchor":"الكبرى نار الكفار في الطبقة السفلى من جهنم والصغرى نار المذنبين في الطبقة العليا من جهنم وهو معنى قول الفراء"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:2","rows":[{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hamd is praise of the praised one’s beautiful attributes and actions, while shukr is praise for a favor; every shukr is hamd but not every hamd is shukr, so God may praise Himself but not thank Himself.","anchor":"فهو الثناء على المحمود بجميل صفاته وأفعاله والشكر الثناء عليه بإنعامه فكل شكر حمد وليس كل حمد شكرا"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hamd differs from madh: hamd is deserved only for a good act, while madh may praise an act or a non-action; all hamd is madh, but not vice versa.","anchor":"أن الحمد لا يستحق إلا على فعل حسن والمدح قد يكون على فعل وغير فعل فكل حمد مدح وليس كل مدح حمدا"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God may be praised for knowledge and power but not hamd for them, since they are attributes of essence; He may be praised and hamd for creating and providing, attributes of action.","anchor":"جاز أن يمدح الله تعالى على صفته بأنه عالم قادر ولم يجز أن يحمد به لأن العلم والقدرة من صفات ذاته"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One derivation of rabb is owner, as in the owner of a house.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من المالك كما يقال رب الدار أي مالكها"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another derivation is master; 12:41 calls a human master rabb.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من السيد لأن السيد يسمى ربا قال تعالى أما أحدكما فيسقي ربه خمرا","mentions":["12:41"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third meaning is manager; rabbani scholars are so called for managing people through knowledge, and a housewife is called rabbat al-bayt for managing the home.","anchor":"أن الرب المدبر ومنه قول الله عز وجل والربانيون والأحبار وهم العلماء سموا ربانيين لقيامهم بتدبير الناس بعلمهم","mentions":["5:44"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth derivation connects rabb to nurturing; stepchildren are named rabائب because the husband raises them, as in 4:23.","anchor":"الرب مشتق من التربية ومنه قوله تعالى وربائبكم اللاتي في حجوركم فسمي ولد الزوجة ربيبة لتربية الزوج لها","mentions":["4:23"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"If rabb means owner or master, it describes God’s essence; if it means manager or nurturer, it describes His action.","anchor":"فعلى هذا أن صفة الله تعالى بأنه رب لأنه مالك أو سيد فذلك صفة من صفات ذاته وإن قيل لأنه مدبر لخلقه أو مربيهم"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"With the definite article, rabb is exclusive to God; without it, the word is shared by God and His servants.","anchor":"ومتى أدخلت عليه الألف واللام اختص الله تعالى به دون عباده وإن حذفتا منه صار مشتركا بين الله وبين عباده"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-alamin is the plural of alam, with no singular of the same form, like raht and qawm; each age or community is an alam, as the cited al-A‘raj verse illustrates.","anchor":"فهو جمع عالم لا واحد له من لفظه مثل رهط وقوم وأهل كل زمان عالم قال العجاج"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas takes the worlds to mean rational beings: angels, humans, and jinn.","anchor":"أنه ما يعقل من الملائكة والإنس والجن وهذا قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view takes the worlds to mean the present world and all it contains.","anchor":"أن العالم الدنيا وما فيها"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"أبو إسحاق الزجاج","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Zajjaj takes the worlds to include everything God created in this world and the afterlife.","anchor":"أن العالم كل ما خلقه الله تعالى في الدنيا والآخرة وهذا قول أبي إسحاق الزجاج"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The derivation from knowledge fits the interpretation that alam means rational beings.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من العلم وهذا تأويل من جعل العالم اسما لما يعقل"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The alternative derivation is from sign, since the worlds are signs pointing to their creator; this fits the interpretation that alam means all created things.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من العلامة لأنه دلالة على خالقه وهذا تأويل من جعل العالم اسما لكل مخلوق"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:3","rows":[],"none":"verse text only"}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:5","rows":[{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["إِيَّاكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الخليل","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Khalil says the divine name is annexed to the pronoun kaf in iyyaka.","anchor":"أن اسم الله تعالى مضاف إلى الكاف وهذا قول الخليل"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["إِيَّاكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الأخفش","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Akhfash takes iyyaka as a single pronoun for God, not an annexation, because a pronoun is not annexed.","anchor":"أنها كلمة واحدة كني بها عن اسم الله تعالى وليس فيها إضافة لأن المضمر لا يضاف وهذا قول الأخفش"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"prefers","claim":"The clearest sense of worship is humility, the highest form of submission, owed only to God as giver of the greatest gifts such as life, reason, hearing, and sight.","anchor":"أن العبادة الخضوع ولا يستحقها إلا الله تعالى لأنها أعلى مراتب الخضوع فلا يستحقها إلا المنعم بأعظم النعم"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A second interpretation takes worship to mean obedience.","anchor":"أن العبادة الطاعة"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third interpretation takes worship to mean drawing near through obedience.","anchor":"أنها التقرب بالطاعة"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Humility is clearest because Christians worshipped Jesus without obeying him through worship, while the Prophet is obeyed but is not thereby worshipped.","anchor":"لأن النصارى عبدت عيسى عليه السلام ولم تطعه بالعبادة والنبي صلى الله عليه وسلم مطاع وليس بمعبود بالطاعة"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:6","rows":[{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation of ihdina is guide us and show us the way.","anchor":"معناه أرشدنا ودلنا"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas interprets ihdina as grant us success.","anchor":"معناه وفقنا وهذا قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Sirat can mean the straight path, illustrated by Jarir’s verse about the commander being on a straight course when routes bend.","anchor":"أنه السبيل المستقيم ومنه قول جرير أمير المؤمنين على صراط إذا اعوج الموارد مستقيم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Sirat can also mean a clear road, as in 7:86 and the cited verse about turning from the clear path.","anchor":"أنه الطريق الواضح ومنه قوله تعالى ولا تقعدوا بكل صراط توعدون وقال الشاعر","mentions":["7:86"]},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Sirat derives from the passage of food as it moves through the throat.","anchor":"وهو مشتق من مسترط الطعام وهو ممره في الحلق"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The already guided ask for guidance to continue and remain constant.","anchor":"أنهم دعوا باستدامة الهداية وإن كانوا قد هدوا"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Alternatively, the prayer asks God to increase their guidance.","anchor":"معناه زدنا هداية"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third view sees the request as sincere desire for guidance and hope for the reward of prayer.","anchor":"دعوا بها إخلاصا للرغبة ورجاء لثواب الدعاء"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"علي وعبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Ali and Abdullah identify the straight path as God’s Book; a similar interpretation is attributed to the Prophet.","anchor":"أنه كتاب الله تعالى وهو قول علي وعبد الله ويروى نحوه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"A report attributed to the Prophet likewise identifies the straight path as God’s Book; no grading is given.","anchor":"ويروى نحوه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"جابر بن عبد الله ومحمد بن الحنفية","stance":"reports","claim":"Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya identify the straight path as Islam.","anchor":"أنه الإسلام وهو قول جابر بن عبد الله ومحمد بن الحنفية"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas identifies it as the way guiding to God’s religion, without any crookedness.","anchor":"أنه الطريق الهادي إلى دين الله تعالى الذي لا عوج فيه وهو قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"الحسن البصري وأبو العالية الرياحي","stance":"reports","claim":"Hasan al-Basri and Abu al-Aliya al-Riyahi identify the path as the Messenger and the best of his family and Companions.","anchor":"هو رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وأخيار أهل بيته وأصحابه وهو قول الحسن البصري وأبي العالية الرياحي"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:7","rows":[{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One view identifies those favored as the angels.","anchor":"أحدها أنهم الملائكة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view identifies those favored as the prophets.","anchor":"والثاني أنهم الأنبياء"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view identifies them as believers in earlier scriptures.","anchor":"والثالث أنهم المؤمنون بالكتب السالفة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"وكيع","stance":"reports","claim":"Waki‘ identifies them as Muslims.","anchor":"والرابع أنهم المسلمون وهو قول وكيع"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"عبد الرحمن بن زيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd identifies them as the Prophet and his Companions.","anchor":"هم النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ومن معه من أصحابه وهذا قول عبد الرحمن بن زيد"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["صِرَٰطَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"عمر بن الخطاب وعبد الله بن الزبير","stance":"reports","claim":"Umar ibn al-Khattab and Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr read min an‘amta alayhim instead of alladhina an‘amta alayhim.","anchor":"وقرأ عمر بن الخطاب وعبد الله بن الزبير صراط من أنعمت عليهم"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عدي بن حاتم","stance":"reports","claim":"Adi ibn Hatim reports that the Prophet identified those under wrath as Jews and those astray as Christians; al-Mawardi says all exegetes agree.","anchor":"روى عن عدي بن حاتم قال سألت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم عن المغضوب عليهم فقال هم اليهود وعن الضالين فقال هم النصارى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-Mawardi says all exegetes agree that those under wrath are Jews and those astray are Christians.","anchor":"وهو قول جميع المفسرين"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation takes God’s wrath in its familiar sense as anger among people.","anchor":"الغضب المعروف من العباد"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation takes wrath as the will to exact vengeance, since the linguistic root implies harshness, which cannot be ascribed to God.","anchor":"أنه إرادة الانتقام لأن أصل الغضب في اللغة هو الغلظة وهذه الصفة لا تجوز على الله تعالى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third interpretation is that God’s wrath means His condemnation of them.","anchor":"أن غضبه عليهم هو ذمه لهم"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth interprets wrath as a kind of punishment named anger, just as God’s blessings are named mercy.","anchor":"أنه نوع من العقوبة سمي غضبا كما سميت نعمه رحمة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلضَّآلِّينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Misguidance is the opposite of guidance.","anchor":"والضلال ضد الهدى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God singles out Jews as the objects of wrath because they are the most hostile.","anchor":"وخص الله تعالى اليهود بالغضب لأنهم أشد عداوة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"عمر بن الخطاب","stance":"reports","claim":"Umar ibn al-Khattab reads ghayr before al-dallin as well, repeating ghayr in the phrase.","anchor":"وقرأ عمر بن الخطاب غير المغضوب عليهم وغير الضالين"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:1","rows":[{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["*"],"type":"sciences","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-A‘la is Meccan by agreement.","anchor":"سورة الأعلى مكية باتفاق"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس والسدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas and al-Suddi interpret sabbih as glorify your Lord Most High; ism is an added word intended to exalt the named one, as Labid’s verse illustrates.","anchor":"عظم ربك الأعلى قاله ابن عباس والسدي والاسم صلة قصد بها تعظيم المسمى كما قال لبيد"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الطبري","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Tabari interprets the command as declaring the Lord’s name too exalted to be given to anyone else.","anchor":"نزه اسم ربك عن أن يسمى به أحد سواه ذكره الطبري"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation is to raise one’s voice in remembrance of the Lord, supported by Jarir’s verse about pilgrims chanting and magnifying God.","anchor":"معناه ارفع صوتك بذكر ربك قال جرير قبح الإله وجوه تغلب كلما سبح الحجيج وكبروا تكبيرا"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth interpretation is pray to your Lord.","anchor":"الرابع صل لربك"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"On the prayer interpretation, ism rabbika can mean by your Lord’s command.","anchor":"بأمر ربك"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"It can instead mean by mentioning your Lord at the opening of prayer.","anchor":"بذكر ربك أن تفتتح به الصلاة"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"It can also mean keeping the Lord in one’s heart while intending the prayer.","anchor":"أن تكون ذاكرا لربك بقلبك في نيتك للصلاة"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"علي وابن عباس وابن عمر","stance":"reports","claim":"Ali, Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Umar would say Glory be to my Lord Most High when beginning the sura’s recitation, acting on its opening command.","anchor":"وروي أن عليا وابن عباس وابن عمر كانوا إذا افتتحوا قراءة هذه السورة قالوا سبحان ربي الأعلى امتثالا لأمره تعالى في ابتدائها"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبي وابن عمر","stance":"reports","claim":"It is said that Ubay’s reading has Glory be to my Lord Most High in place of the opening words, and Ibn Umar recited it that way.","anchor":"وقيل إنها في قراءة أبي سبحان ربي الأعلى وكان ابن عمر يقرؤها كذلك"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:2","rows":[{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One possibility is that God brought people into being and then perfected them.","anchor":"يعني أنشأ خلقهم ثم سواهم فأكملهم"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another is that He created them fully and made each limb proportionate to its counterpart.","anchor":"خلقهم خلقا كاملا وسوى لكل جارحة مثلا"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third is that He created them through His favor and equalized them in His rulings; al-Dahhak specifies that He created Adam and fashioned his form.","anchor":"خلقهم بإنعامه وسوى بينهم في أحكامه قال الضحاك خلق آدم فسوى خلقه"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth possibility is that He created in men’s loins and fashioned in mothers’ wombs.","anchor":"خلق في أصلاب الرجال وسوى في أرحام الأمهات"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fifth possibility is that He created bodies and fashioned understandings.","anchor":"خلق الأجساد فسوى الأفهام"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:3","rows":[{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujahid says God decreed misery and happiness, and guided toward right conduct and misguidance.","anchor":"قدر الشقاوة والسعادة وهداه للرشد والضلالة قاله مجاهد"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view says God apportioned provisions and food, and guided humans to their livelihood and wild animals to their pastures.","anchor":"قدر أرزاقهم وأقواتهم وهداهم لمعاشهم إن كانوا إنسا ولمراعيهم إن كانوا وحشا"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"السدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Suddi says God made them male and female and guided the male in approaching the female.","anchor":"قدرهم ذكورا وإناثا وهدى الذكر كيف يأتي الأنثى قاله السدي"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth possibility is that God determined their formation in the womb and guided them to emerge fully formed.","anchor":"قدر خلقهم في الأرحام وهداهم الخروج للتمام"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fifth possibility is that God created them for recompense and guided them to action.","anchor":"خلقهم للجزاء وهداهم للعمل"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:6","rows":[{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["فَلَا تَنسَىٰٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation takes do not forget to mean do not abandon the work, except where God grants a concession; on this reading the phrase prohibits associating partners with God.","anchor":"أن معنى قوله فلا تنسى أي فلا تترك العمل إلا ما شاء الله أن يترخص لك فيه فعلى هذا التأويل يكون هذا نهيا عن الشرك"},{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["سَنُقْرِئُكَ فَلَا تَنسَىٰٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The other interpretation is God’s assurance that the Prophet will not forget the Qur’an He recites to him.","anchor":"أنه إخبار من الله تعالى أنه لا ينسى ما يقرئه من القرآن"},{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["سَنُقْرِئُكَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas relates that the Prophet repeated Gabriel’s revelation for fear of forgetting, so God revealed that He would recite the Qur’an to him and he would not forget; no grading is given.","anchor":"حكى ابن عباس أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم كان إذا نزل عليه جبريل بالوحي يقرؤه خيفة أن ينساه فأنزل الله تعالى سنقرئك فلا تنسى"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:12","rows":[{"verses":["87:12"],"words":["ٱلنَّارَ ٱلْكُبْرَىٰ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"يحيى بن سلام","stance":"reports","claim":"Yahya ibn Sallam identifies the greater fire as Hell and the lesser fire as the fire of this world.","anchor":"هي نار جهنم والصغرى نار الدنيا قاله يحيى بن سلام"},{"verses":["87:12"],"words":["ٱلنَّارَ ٱلْكُبْرَىٰ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farra’s interpretation identifies the greater fire as the disbelievers’ fire in Hell’s lowest level and the lesser fire as sinners’ fire in its upper level.","anchor":"الكبرى نار الكفار في الطبقة السفلى من جهنم والصغرى نار المذنبين في الطبقة العليا من جهنم وهو معنى قول الفراء"}]}

{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:2","rows":[{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hamd is praise of the praised one’s beautiful attributes and actions, while shukr is praise for a favor; every shukr is hamd but not every hamd is shukr, so God may praise Himself but not thank Himself.","anchor":"فهو الثناء على المحمود بجميل صفاته وأفعاله والشكر الثناء عليه بإنعامه فكل شكر حمد وليس كل حمد شكرا"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hamd differs from madh: hamd is deserved only for a good act, while madh may praise an act or a non-action; all hamd is madh, but not vice versa.","anchor":"أن الحمد لا يستحق إلا على فعل حسن والمدح قد يكون على فعل وغير فعل فكل حمد مدح وليس كل مدح حمدا"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God may be praised for knowledge and power but not hamd for them, since they are attributes of essence; He may be praised and hamd for creating and providing, attributes of action.","anchor":"جاز أن يمدح الله تعالى على صفته بأنه عالم قادر ولم يجز أن يحمد به لأن العلم والقدرة من صفات ذاته"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One derivation of rabb is owner, as in the owner of a house.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من المالك كما يقال رب الدار أي مالكها"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another derivation is master; 12:41 calls a human master rabb.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من السيد لأن السيد يسمى ربا قال تعالى أما أحدكما فيسقي ربه خمرا","mentions":["12:41"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third meaning is manager; rabbani scholars are so called for managing people through knowledge, and a housewife is called rabbat al-bayt for managing the home.","anchor":"أن الرب المدبر ومنه قول الله عز وجل والربانيون والأحبار وهم العلماء سموا ربانيين لقيامهم بتدبير الناس بعلمهم","mentions":["5:44"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth derivation connects rabb to nurturing; stepchildren are named rabائب because the husband raises them, as in 4:23.","anchor":"الرب مشتق من التربية ومنه قوله تعالى وربائبكم اللاتي في حجوركم فسمي ولد الزوجة ربيبة لتربية الزوج لها","mentions":["4:23"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"If rabb means owner or master, it describes God’s essence; if it means manager or nurturer, it describes His action.","anchor":"فعلى هذا أن صفة الله تعالى بأنه رب لأنه مالك أو سيد فذلك صفة من صفات ذاته وإن قيل لأنه مدبر لخلقه أو مربيهم"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"With the definite article, rabb is exclusive to God; without it, the word is shared by God and His servants.","anchor":"ومتى أدخلت عليه الألف واللام اختص الله تعالى به دون عباده وإن حذفتا منه صار مشتركا بين الله وبين عباده"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-alamin is the plural of alam, with no singular of the same form, like raht and qawm; each age or community is an alam, as the cited al-A‘raj verse illustrates.","anchor":"فهو جمع عالم لا واحد له من لفظه مثل رهط وقوم وأهل كل زمان عالم قال العجاج"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas takes the worlds to mean rational beings: angels, humans, and jinn.","anchor":"أنه ما يعقل من الملائكة والإنس والجن وهذا قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view takes the worlds to mean the present world and all it contains.","anchor":"أن العالم الدنيا وما فيها"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"أبو إسحاق الزجاج","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Zajjaj takes the worlds to include everything God created in this world and the afterlife.","anchor":"أن العالم كل ما خلقه الله تعالى في الدنيا والآخرة وهذا قول أبي إسحاق الزجاج"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The derivation from knowledge fits the interpretation that alam means rational beings.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من العلم وهذا تأويل من جعل العالم اسما لما يعقل"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The alternative derivation is from sign, since the worlds are signs pointing to their creator; this fits the interpretation that alam means all created things.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من العلامة لأنه دلالة على خالقه وهذا تأويل من جعل العالم اسما لكل مخلوق"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:3","rows":[],"none":"verse text only"}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:5","rows":[{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["إِيَّاكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الخليل","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Khalil says the divine name is annexed to the pronoun kaf in iyyaka.","anchor":"أن اسم الله تعالى مضاف إلى الكاف وهذا قول الخليل"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["إِيَّاكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الأخفش","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Akhfash takes iyyaka as a single pronoun for God, not an annexation, because a pronoun is not annexed.","anchor":"أنها كلمة واحدة كني بها عن اسم الله تعالى وليس فيها إضافة لأن المضمر لا يضاف وهذا قول الأخفش"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"prefers","claim":"The clearest sense of worship is humility, the highest form of submission, owed only to God as giver of the greatest gifts such as life, reason, hearing, and sight.","anchor":"أن العبادة الخضوع ولا يستحقها إلا الله تعالى لأنها أعلى مراتب الخضوع فلا يستحقها إلا المنعم بأعظم النعم"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A second interpretation takes worship to mean obedience.","anchor":"أن العبادة الطاعة"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third interpretation takes worship to mean drawing near through obedience.","anchor":"أنها التقرب بالطاعة"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Humility is clearest because Christians worshipped Jesus without obeying him through worship, while the Prophet is obeyed but is not thereby worshipped.","anchor":"لأن النصارى عبدت عيسى عليه السلام ولم تطعه بالعبادة والنبي صلى الله عليه وسلم مطاع وليس بمعبود بالطاعة"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:6","rows":[{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation of ihdina is guide us and show us the way.","anchor":"معناه أرشدنا ودلنا"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas interprets ihdina as grant us success.","anchor":"معناه وفقنا وهذا قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Sirat can mean the straight path, illustrated by Jarir’s verse about the commander being on a straight course when routes bend.","anchor":"أنه السبيل المستقيم ومنه قول جرير أمير المؤمنين على صراط إذا اعوج الموارد مستقيم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Sirat can also mean a clear road, as in 7:86 and the cited verse about turning from the clear path.","anchor":"أنه الطريق الواضح ومنه قوله تعالى ولا تقعدوا بكل صراط توعدون وقال الشاعر","mentions":["7:86"]},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Sirat derives from the passage of food as it moves through the throat.","anchor":"وهو مشتق من مسترط الطعام وهو ممره في الحلق"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The already guided ask for guidance to continue and remain constant.","anchor":"أنهم دعوا باستدامة الهداية وإن كانوا قد هدوا"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Alternatively, the prayer asks God to increase their guidance.","anchor":"معناه زدنا هداية"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third view sees the request as sincere desire for guidance and hope for the reward of prayer.","anchor":"دعوا بها إخلاصا للرغبة ورجاء لثواب الدعاء"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"علي وعبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Ali and Abdullah identify the straight path as God’s Book; a similar interpretation is attributed to the Prophet.","anchor":"أنه كتاب الله تعالى وهو قول علي وعبد الله ويروى نحوه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"A report attributed to the Prophet likewise identifies the straight path as God’s Book; no grading is given.","anchor":"ويروى نحوه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"جابر بن عبد الله ومحمد بن الحنفية","stance":"reports","claim":"Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya identify the straight path as Islam.","anchor":"أنه الإسلام وهو قول جابر بن عبد الله ومحمد بن الحنفية"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas identifies it as the way guiding to God’s religion, without any crookedness.","anchor":"أنه الطريق الهادي إلى دين الله تعالى الذي لا عوج فيه وهو قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"الحسن البصري وأبو العالية الرياحي","stance":"reports","claim":"Hasan al-Basri and Abu al-Aliya al-Riyahi identify the path as the Messenger and the best of his family and Companions.","anchor":"هو رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وأخيار أهل بيته وأصحابه وهو قول الحسن البصري وأبي العالية الرياحي"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:7","rows":[{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One view identifies those favored as the angels.","anchor":"أحدها أنهم الملائكة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view identifies those favored as the prophets.","anchor":"والثاني أنهم الأنبياء"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view identifies them as believers in earlier scriptures.","anchor":"والثالث أنهم المؤمنون بالكتب السالفة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"وكيع","stance":"reports","claim":"Waki‘ identifies them as Muslims.","anchor":"والرابع أنهم المسلمون وهو قول وكيع"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"عبد الرحمن بن زيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd identifies them as the Prophet and his Companions.","anchor":"هم النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ومن معه من أصحابه وهذا قول عبد الرحمن بن زيد"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["صِرَٰطَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"عمر بن الخطاب وعبد الله بن الزبير","stance":"reports","claim":"Umar ibn al-Khattab and Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr read min an‘amta alayhim instead of alladhina an‘amta alayhim.","anchor":"وقرأ عمر بن الخطاب وعبد الله بن الزبير صراط من أنعمت عليهم"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عدي بن حاتم","stance":"reports","claim":"Adi ibn Hatim reports that the Prophet identified those under wrath as Jews and those astray as Christians; al-Mawardi says all exegetes agree.","anchor":"روى عن عدي بن حاتم قال سألت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم عن المغضوب عليهم فقال هم اليهود وعن الضالين فقال هم النصارى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-Mawardi says all exegetes agree that those under wrath are Jews and those astray are Christians.","anchor":"وهو قول جميع المفسرين"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation takes God’s wrath in its familiar sense as anger among people.","anchor":"الغضب المعروف من العباد"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation takes wrath as the will to exact vengeance, since the linguistic root implies harshness, which cannot be ascribed to God.","anchor":"أنه إرادة الانتقام لأن أصل الغضب في اللغة هو الغلظة وهذه الصفة لا تجوز على الله تعالى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third interpretation is that God’s wrath means His condemnation of them.","anchor":"أن غضبه عليهم هو ذمه لهم"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth interprets wrath as a kind of punishment named anger, just as God’s blessings are named mercy.","anchor":"أنه نوع من العقوبة سمي غضبا كما سميت نعمه رحمة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلضَّآلِّينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Misguidance is the opposite of guidance.","anchor":"والضلال ضد الهدى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God singles out Jews as the objects of wrath because they are the most hostile.","anchor":"وخص الله تعالى اليهود بالغضب لأنهم أشد عداوة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"عمر بن الخطاب","stance":"reports","claim":"Umar ibn al-Khattab reads ghayr before al-dallin as well, repeating ghayr in the phrase.","anchor":"وقرأ عمر بن الخطاب غير المغضوب عليهم وغير الضالين"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:1","rows":[{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["*"],"type":"sciences","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-A‘la is Meccan by agreement.","anchor":"سورة الأعلى مكية باتفاق"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس والسدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas and al-Suddi interpret sabbih as glorify your Lord Most High; ism is an added word intended to exalt the named one, as Labid’s verse illustrates.","anchor":"عظم ربك الأعلى قاله ابن عباس والسدي والاسم صلة قصد بها تعظيم المسمى كما قال لبيد"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الطبري","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Tabari interprets the command as declaring the Lord’s name too exalted to be given to anyone else.","anchor":"نزه اسم ربك عن أن يسمى به أحد سواه ذكره الطبري"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation is to raise one’s voice in remembrance of the Lord, supported by Jarir’s verse about pilgrims chanting and magnifying God.","anchor":"معناه ارفع صوتك بذكر ربك قال جرير قبح الإله وجوه تغلب كلما سبح الحجيج وكبروا تكبيرا"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth interpretation is pray to your Lord.","anchor":"الرابع صل لربك"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"On the prayer interpretation, ism rabbika can mean by your Lord’s command.","anchor":"بأمر ربك"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"It can instead mean by mentioning your Lord at the opening of prayer.","anchor":"بذكر ربك أن تفتتح به الصلاة"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"It can also mean keeping the Lord in one’s heart while intending the prayer.","anchor":"أن تكون ذاكرا لربك بقلبك في نيتك للصلاة"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"علي وابن عباس وابن عمر","stance":"reports","claim":"Ali, Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Umar would say Glory be to my Lord Most High when beginning the sura’s recitation, acting on its opening command.","anchor":"وروي أن عليا وابن عباس وابن عمر كانوا إذا افتتحوا قراءة هذه السورة قالوا سبحان ربي الأعلى امتثالا لأمره تعالى في ابتدائها"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبي وابن عمر","stance":"reports","claim":"It is said that Ubay’s reading has Glory be to my Lord Most High in place of the opening words, and Ibn Umar recited it that way.","anchor":"وقيل إنها في قراءة أبي سبحان ربي الأعلى وكان ابن عمر يقرؤها كذلك"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:2","rows":[{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One possibility is that God brought people into being and then perfected them.","anchor":"يعني أنشأ خلقهم ثم سواهم فأكملهم"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another is that He created them fully and made each limb proportionate to its counterpart.","anchor":"خلقهم خلقا كاملا وسوى لكل جارحة مثلا"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third is that He created them through His favor and equalized them in His rulings; al-Dahhak specifies that He created Adam and fashioned his form.","anchor":"خلقهم بإنعامه وسوى بينهم في أحكامه قال الضحاك خلق آدم فسوى خلقه"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth possibility is that He created in men’s loins and fashioned in mothers’ wombs.","anchor":"خلق في أصلاب الرجال وسوى في أرحام الأمهات"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fifth possibility is that He created bodies and fashioned understandings.","anchor":"خلق الأجساد فسوى الأفهام"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:3","rows":[{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujahid says God decreed misery and happiness, and guided toward right conduct and misguidance.","anchor":"قدر الشقاوة والسعادة وهداه للرشد والضلالة قاله مجاهد"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view says God apportioned provisions and food, and guided humans to their livelihood and wild animals to their pastures.","anchor":"قدر أرزاقهم وأقواتهم وهداهم لمعاشهم إن كانوا إنسا ولمراعيهم إن كانوا وحشا"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"السدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Suddi says God made them male and female and guided the male in approaching the female.","anchor":"قدرهم ذكورا وإناثا وهدى الذكر كيف يأتي الأنثى قاله السدي"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth possibility is that God determined their formation in the womb and guided them to emerge fully formed.","anchor":"قدر خلقهم في الأرحام وهداهم الخروج للتمام"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fifth possibility is that God created them for recompense and guided them to action.","anchor":"خلقهم للجزاء وهداهم للعمل"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:6","rows":[{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["فَلَا تَنسَىٰٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation takes do not forget to mean do not abandon the work, except where God grants a concession; on this reading the phrase prohibits associating partners with God.","anchor":"أن معنى قوله فلا تنسى أي فلا تترك العمل إلا ما شاء الله أن يترخص لك فيه فعلى هذا التأويل يكون هذا نهيا عن الشرك"},{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["سَنُقْرِئُكَ فَلَا تَنسَىٰٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The other interpretation is God’s assurance that the Prophet will not forget the Qur’an He recites to him.","anchor":"أنه إخبار من الله تعالى أنه لا ينسى ما يقرئه من القرآن"},{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["سَنُقْرِئُكَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas relates that the Prophet repeated Gabriel’s revelation for fear of forgetting, so God revealed that He would recite the Qur’an to him and he would not forget; no grading is given.","anchor":"حكى ابن عباس أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم كان إذا نزل عليه جبريل بالوحي يقرؤه خيفة أن ينساه فأنزل الله تعالى سنقرئك فلا تنسى"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:12","rows":[{"verses":["87:12"],"words":["ٱلنَّارَ ٱلْكُبْرَىٰ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"يحيى بن سلام","stance":"reports","claim":"Yahya ibn Sallam identifies the greater fire as Hell and the lesser fire as the fire of this world.","anchor":"هي نار جهنم والصغرى نار الدنيا قاله يحيى بن سلام"},{"verses":["87:12"],"words":["ٱلنَّارَ ٱلْكُبْرَىٰ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farra’s interpretation identifies the greater fire as the disbelievers’ fire in Hell’s lowest level and the lesser fire as sinners’ fire in its upper level.","anchor":"الكبرى نار الكفار في الطبقة السفلى من جهنم والصغرى نار المذنبين في الطبقة العليا من جهنم وهو معنى قول الفراء"}]}

{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:2","rows":[{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hamd is praise of the praised one’s beautiful attributes and actions, while shukr is praise for a favor; every shukr is hamd but not every hamd is shukr, so God may praise Himself but not thank Himself.","anchor":"فهو الثناء على المحمود بجميل صفاته وأفعاله والشكر الثناء عليه بإنعامه فكل شكر حمد وليس كل حمد شكرا"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Hamd differs from madh: hamd is deserved only for a good act, while madh may praise an act or a non-action; all hamd is madh, but not vice versa.","anchor":"أن الحمد لا يستحق إلا على فعل حسن والمدح قد يكون على فعل وغير فعل فكل حمد مدح وليس كل مدح حمدا"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God may be praised for knowledge and power but not hamd for them, since they are attributes of essence; He may be praised and hamd for creating and providing, attributes of action.","anchor":"جاز أن يمدح الله تعالى على صفته بأنه عالم قادر ولم يجز أن يحمد به لأن العلم والقدرة من صفات ذاته"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One derivation of rabb is owner, as in the owner of a house.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من المالك كما يقال رب الدار أي مالكها"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another derivation is master; 12:41 calls a human master rabb.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من السيد لأن السيد يسمى ربا قال تعالى أما أحدكما فيسقي ربه خمرا","mentions":["12:41"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third meaning is manager; rabbani scholars are so called for managing people through knowledge, and a housewife is called rabbat al-bayt for managing the home.","anchor":"أن الرب المدبر ومنه قول الله عز وجل والربانيون والأحبار وهم العلماء سموا ربانيين لقيامهم بتدبير الناس بعلمهم","mentions":["5:44"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth derivation connects rabb to nurturing; stepchildren are named rabائب because the husband raises them, as in 4:23.","anchor":"الرب مشتق من التربية ومنه قوله تعالى وربائبكم اللاتي في حجوركم فسمي ولد الزوجة ربيبة لتربية الزوج لها","mentions":["4:23"]},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"If rabb means owner or master, it describes God’s essence; if it means manager or nurturer, it describes His action.","anchor":"فعلى هذا أن صفة الله تعالى بأنه رب لأنه مالك أو سيد فذلك صفة من صفات ذاته وإن قيل لأنه مدبر لخلقه أو مربيهم"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["رَبِّ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"With the definite article, rabb is exclusive to God; without it, the word is shared by God and His servants.","anchor":"ومتى أدخلت عليه الألف واللام اختص الله تعالى به دون عباده وإن حذفتا منه صار مشتركا بين الله وبين عباده"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-alamin is the plural of alam, with no singular of the same form, like raht and qawm; each age or community is an alam, as the cited al-A‘raj verse illustrates.","anchor":"فهو جمع عالم لا واحد له من لفظه مثل رهط وقوم وأهل كل زمان عالم قال العجاج"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas takes the worlds to mean rational beings: angels, humans, and jinn.","anchor":"أنه ما يعقل من الملائكة والإنس والجن وهذا قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view takes the worlds to mean the present world and all it contains.","anchor":"أن العالم الدنيا وما فيها"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"أبو إسحاق الزجاج","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Zajjaj takes the worlds to include everything God created in this world and the afterlife.","anchor":"أن العالم كل ما خلقه الله تعالى في الدنيا والآخرة وهذا قول أبي إسحاق الزجاج"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The derivation from knowledge fits the interpretation that alam means rational beings.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من العلم وهذا تأويل من جعل العالم اسما لما يعقل"},{"verses":["1:2"],"words":["ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The alternative derivation is from sign, since the worlds are signs pointing to their creator; this fits the interpretation that alam means all created things.","anchor":"أنه مشتق من العلامة لأنه دلالة على خالقه وهذا تأويل من جعل العالم اسما لكل مخلوق"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:3","rows":[],"none":"verse text only"}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:5","rows":[{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["إِيَّاكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الخليل","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Khalil says the divine name is annexed to the pronoun kaf in iyyaka.","anchor":"أن اسم الله تعالى مضاف إلى الكاف وهذا قول الخليل"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["إِيَّاكَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الأخفش","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Akhfash takes iyyaka as a single pronoun for God, not an annexation, because a pronoun is not annexed.","anchor":"أنها كلمة واحدة كني بها عن اسم الله تعالى وليس فيها إضافة لأن المضمر لا يضاف وهذا قول الأخفش"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"prefers","claim":"The clearest sense of worship is humility, the highest form of submission, owed only to God as giver of the greatest gifts such as life, reason, hearing, and sight.","anchor":"أن العبادة الخضوع ولا يستحقها إلا الله تعالى لأنها أعلى مراتب الخضوع فلا يستحقها إلا المنعم بأعظم النعم"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A second interpretation takes worship to mean obedience.","anchor":"أن العبادة الطاعة"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third interpretation takes worship to mean drawing near through obedience.","anchor":"أنها التقرب بالطاعة"},{"verses":["1:5"],"words":["نَعْبُدُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Humility is clearest because Christians worshipped Jesus without obeying him through worship, while the Prophet is obeyed but is not thereby worshipped.","anchor":"لأن النصارى عبدت عيسى عليه السلام ولم تطعه بالعبادة والنبي صلى الله عليه وسلم مطاع وليس بمعبود بالطاعة"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:6","rows":[{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation of ihdina is guide us and show us the way.","anchor":"معناه أرشدنا ودلنا"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas interprets ihdina as grant us success.","anchor":"معناه وفقنا وهذا قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Sirat can mean the straight path, illustrated by Jarir’s verse about the commander being on a straight course when routes bend.","anchor":"أنه السبيل المستقيم ومنه قول جرير أمير المؤمنين على صراط إذا اعوج الموارد مستقيم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Sirat can also mean a clear road, as in 7:86 and the cited verse about turning from the clear path.","anchor":"أنه الطريق الواضح ومنه قوله تعالى ولا تقعدوا بكل صراط توعدون وقال الشاعر","mentions":["7:86"]},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Sirat derives from the passage of food as it moves through the throat.","anchor":"وهو مشتق من مسترط الطعام وهو ممره في الحلق"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The already guided ask for guidance to continue and remain constant.","anchor":"أنهم دعوا باستدامة الهداية وإن كانوا قد هدوا"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Alternatively, the prayer asks God to increase their guidance.","anchor":"معناه زدنا هداية"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱهْدِنَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third view sees the request as sincere desire for guidance and hope for the reward of prayer.","anchor":"دعوا بها إخلاصا للرغبة ورجاء لثواب الدعاء"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"علي وعبد الله","stance":"reports","claim":"Ali and Abdullah identify the straight path as God’s Book; a similar interpretation is attributed to the Prophet.","anchor":"أنه كتاب الله تعالى وهو قول علي وعبد الله ويروى نحوه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"A report attributed to the Prophet likewise identifies the straight path as God’s Book; no grading is given.","anchor":"ويروى نحوه عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"جابر بن عبد الله ومحمد بن الحنفية","stance":"reports","claim":"Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya identify the straight path as Islam.","anchor":"أنه الإسلام وهو قول جابر بن عبد الله ومحمد بن الحنفية"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas identifies it as the way guiding to God’s religion, without any crookedness.","anchor":"أنه الطريق الهادي إلى دين الله تعالى الذي لا عوج فيه وهو قول ابن عباس"},{"verses":["1:6"],"words":["ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"الحسن البصري وأبو العالية الرياحي","stance":"reports","claim":"Hasan al-Basri and Abu al-Aliya al-Riyahi identify the path as the Messenger and the best of his family and Companions.","anchor":"هو رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وأخيار أهل بيته وأصحابه وهو قول الحسن البصري وأبي العالية الرياحي"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:1:7","rows":[{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One view identifies those favored as the angels.","anchor":"أحدها أنهم الملائكة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view identifies those favored as the prophets.","anchor":"والثاني أنهم الأنبياء"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view identifies them as believers in earlier scriptures.","anchor":"والثالث أنهم المؤمنون بالكتب السالفة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"وكيع","stance":"reports","claim":"Waki‘ identifies them as Muslims.","anchor":"والرابع أنهم المسلمون وهو قول وكيع"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"عبد الرحمن بن زيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd identifies them as the Prophet and his Companions.","anchor":"هم النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم ومن معه من أصحابه وهذا قول عبد الرحمن بن زيد"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["صِرَٰطَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"عمر بن الخطاب وعبد الله بن الزبير","stance":"reports","claim":"Umar ibn al-Khattab and Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr read min an‘amta alayhim instead of alladhina an‘amta alayhim.","anchor":"وقرأ عمر بن الخطاب وعبد الله بن الزبير صراط من أنعمت عليهم"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عدي بن حاتم","stance":"reports","claim":"Adi ibn Hatim reports that the Prophet identified those under wrath as Jews and those astray as Christians; al-Mawardi says all exegetes agree.","anchor":"روى عن عدي بن حاتم قال سألت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم عن المغضوب عليهم فقال هم اليهود وعن الضالين فقال هم النصارى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-Mawardi says all exegetes agree that those under wrath are Jews and those astray are Christians.","anchor":"وهو قول جميع المفسرين"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation takes God’s wrath in its familiar sense as anger among people.","anchor":"الغضب المعروف من العباد"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation takes wrath as the will to exact vengeance, since the linguistic root implies harshness, which cannot be ascribed to God.","anchor":"أنه إرادة الانتقام لأن أصل الغضب في اللغة هو الغلظة وهذه الصفة لا تجوز على الله تعالى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third interpretation is that God’s wrath means His condemnation of them.","anchor":"أن غضبه عليهم هو ذمه لهم"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth interprets wrath as a kind of punishment named anger, just as God’s blessings are named mercy.","anchor":"أنه نوع من العقوبة سمي غضبا كما سميت نعمه رحمة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلضَّآلِّينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Misguidance is the opposite of guidance.","anchor":"والضلال ضد الهدى"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God singles out Jews as the objects of wrath because they are the most hostile.","anchor":"وخص الله تعالى اليهود بالغضب لأنهم أشد عداوة"},{"verses":["1:7"],"words":["وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"عمر بن الخطاب","stance":"reports","claim":"Umar ibn al-Khattab reads ghayr before al-dallin as well, repeating ghayr in the phrase.","anchor":"وقرأ عمر بن الخطاب غير المغضوب عليهم وغير الضالين"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:1","rows":[{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["*"],"type":"sciences","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-A‘la is Meccan by agreement.","anchor":"سورة الأعلى مكية باتفاق"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس والسدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas and al-Suddi interpret sabbih as glorify your Lord Most High; ism is an added word intended to exalt the named one, as Labid’s verse illustrates.","anchor":"عظم ربك الأعلى قاله ابن عباس والسدي والاسم صلة قصد بها تعظيم المسمى كما قال لبيد"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الطبري","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Tabari interprets the command as declaring the Lord’s name too exalted to be given to anyone else.","anchor":"نزه اسم ربك عن أن يسمى به أحد سواه ذكره الطبري"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation is to raise one’s voice in remembrance of the Lord, supported by Jarir’s verse about pilgrims chanting and magnifying God.","anchor":"معناه ارفع صوتك بذكر ربك قال جرير قبح الإله وجوه تغلب كلما سبح الحجيج وكبروا تكبيرا"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth interpretation is pray to your Lord.","anchor":"الرابع صل لربك"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"On the prayer interpretation, ism rabbika can mean by your Lord’s command.","anchor":"بأمر ربك"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"It can instead mean by mentioning your Lord at the opening of prayer.","anchor":"بذكر ربك أن تفتتح به الصلاة"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["ٱسْمَ رَبِّكَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"It can also mean keeping the Lord in one’s heart while intending the prayer.","anchor":"أن تكون ذاكرا لربك بقلبك في نيتك للصلاة"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"علي وابن عباس وابن عمر","stance":"reports","claim":"Ali, Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Umar would say Glory be to my Lord Most High when beginning the sura’s recitation, acting on its opening command.","anchor":"وروي أن عليا وابن عباس وابن عمر كانوا إذا افتتحوا قراءة هذه السورة قالوا سبحان ربي الأعلى امتثالا لأمره تعالى في ابتدائها"},{"verses":["87:1"],"words":["سَبِّحِ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبي وابن عمر","stance":"reports","claim":"It is said that Ubay’s reading has Glory be to my Lord Most High in place of the opening words, and Ibn Umar recited it that way.","anchor":"وقيل إنها في قراءة أبي سبحان ربي الأعلى وكان ابن عمر يقرؤها كذلك"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:2","rows":[{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One possibility is that God brought people into being and then perfected them.","anchor":"يعني أنشأ خلقهم ثم سواهم فأكملهم"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another is that He created them fully and made each limb proportionate to its counterpart.","anchor":"خلقهم خلقا كاملا وسوى لكل جارحة مثلا"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A third is that He created them through His favor and equalized them in His rulings; al-Dahhak specifies that He created Adam and fashioned his form.","anchor":"خلقهم بإنعامه وسوى بينهم في أحكامه قال الضحاك خلق آدم فسوى خلقه"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth possibility is that He created in men’s loins and fashioned in mothers’ wombs.","anchor":"خلق في أصلاب الرجال وسوى في أرحام الأمهات"},{"verses":["87:2"],"words":["خَلَقَ فَسَوَّىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fifth possibility is that He created bodies and fashioned understandings.","anchor":"خلق الأجساد فسوى الأفهام"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:3","rows":[{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujahid says God decreed misery and happiness, and guided toward right conduct and misguidance.","anchor":"قدر الشقاوة والسعادة وهداه للرشد والضلالة قاله مجاهد"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view says God apportioned provisions and food, and guided humans to their livelihood and wild animals to their pastures.","anchor":"قدر أرزاقهم وأقواتهم وهداهم لمعاشهم إن كانوا إنسا ولمراعيهم إن كانوا وحشا"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"السدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Suddi says God made them male and female and guided the male in approaching the female.","anchor":"قدرهم ذكورا وإناثا وهدى الذكر كيف يأتي الأنثى قاله السدي"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth possibility is that God determined their formation in the womb and guided them to emerge fully formed.","anchor":"قدر خلقهم في الأرحام وهداهم الخروج للتمام"},{"verses":["87:3"],"words":["قَدَّرَ فَهَدَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"A fifth possibility is that God created them for recompense and guided them to action.","anchor":"خلقهم للجزاء وهداهم للعمل"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:6","rows":[{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["فَلَا تَنسَىٰٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"One interpretation takes do not forget to mean do not abandon the work, except where God grants a concession; on this reading the phrase prohibits associating partners with God.","anchor":"أن معنى قوله فلا تنسى أي فلا تترك العمل إلا ما شاء الله أن يترخص لك فيه فعلى هذا التأويل يكون هذا نهيا عن الشرك"},{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["سَنُقْرِئُكَ فَلَا تَنسَىٰٓ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"unattributed","stance":"reports","claim":"The other interpretation is God’s assurance that the Prophet will not forget the Qur’an He recites to him.","anchor":"أنه إخبار من الله تعالى أنه لا ينسى ما يقرئه من القرآن"},{"verses":["87:6"],"words":["سَنُقْرِئُكَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas relates that the Prophet repeated Gabriel’s revelation for fear of forgetting, so God revealed that He would recite the Qur’an to him and he would not forget; no grading is given.","anchor":"حكى ابن عباس أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم كان إذا نزل عليه جبريل بالوحي يقرؤه خيفة أن ينساه فأنزل الله تعالى سنقرئك فلا تنسى"}]}
{"loc":"MAWARDI:87:12","rows":[{"verses":["87:12"],"words":["ٱلنَّارَ ٱلْكُبْرَىٰ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"يحيى بن سلام","stance":"reports","claim":"Yahya ibn Sallam identifies the greater fire as Hell and the lesser fire as the fire of this world.","anchor":"هي نار جهنم والصغرى نار الدنيا قاله يحيى بن سلام"},{"verses":["87:12"],"words":["ٱلنَّارَ ٱلْكُبْرَىٰ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farra’s interpretation identifies the greater fire as the disbelievers’ fire in Hell’s lowest level and the lesser fire as sinners’ fire in its upper level.","anchor":"الكبرى نار الكفار في الطبقة السفلى من جهنم والصغرى نار المذنبين في الطبقة العليا من جهنم وهو معنى قول الفراء"}]}
